  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nTODAY + FRIDAY:\n\nSouthwesterly flow continues to dominate the region, which is \nworking to continuously advect subtropical moisture into western \nColorado and eastern Utah this afternoon. Certain locations in \nsouthwest Colorado and southeast Utah are already overperforming the \nforecast, which means the risk of flash flooding/flooding is ongoing \nin some areas, if not likely to occur. Please continue to stay \nweather aware in the coming hours. Additionally, there is a threat \nfor embedded thunderstorms within these rain showers, particularly \nin the Four Corners area this afternoon. Some storms are capable of \nproducing small hail, gusty winds, and additional heavy rainfall. As \nwe approach sunset, the threat for convective activity gradually \ndiminishes and showers appear to shift to more stratiform in \nnature. Precipitation chances will continue into the overnight \nhours before scattering out by Friday afternoon. Shower and \nthunderstorm chances don't stay away for long as Friday night \ninto Saturday morning will see additional shower and storm activity,\nparticularly south of the I-70 corridor. This is mainly due to \nresidual moisture from the previous system in combination with a\nnew low pressure system forecast to track over the region this \nweekend. \n\n\nTHE WEEKEND + NEXT WEEK:  \n\nModels stay in fairly good agreement through the weekend that \nunsettled weather will remain in the forecast. The timing and \nspecific track of the next low pressure system is still \nuncertain, therefore there are still unknowns. All in all, \nprecipitation chances remain in the forecast this weekend.\n\nAs we move towards next week, models are also in fairly good \nagreement that dry zonal flow will begin to propagate the region by \nMonday. Because of this, we will be seeing cooler than normal \ntemperatures, with the potential for overnight lows to drop \nbelow freezing for a couple hours at a time. Keep in mind, this \nis still far out, so confidence remains low on this matter.",
